    "result_text": "The full suite consists of the single concrete `AcceptanceTest` (AcceptanceBase is abstract), and it's green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `customerCode` assignment on owner creation, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Assignment logic** \u2014 `rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`: injected `OwnerRepository` into the create pipeline's first step and set the code before the owner is saved:\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` (uses fewer if the name is shorter).\n- `NNNN` = `String.format(\"%04d\", ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1)` \u2014 a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count. `BuildOwner` runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the count reflects committed + in-flight state; creating two owners yields consecutive numbers.\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter to `model/Owner.java`, and a nullable `customer_code` column to all four `db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` `owners` tables (existing seed inserts use explicit column lists, so they're unaffected). This makes the code survive the round-trip so the test's `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads it back.\n\n**API exposure** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`; the generated `OwnerDto` picks it up and MapStruct auto-maps it by name (both response paths and the created-response now carry it).\n\nThe acceptance test verifies the `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes and that the two sequence numbers differ by exactly 1 \u2014 both hold.",
